      "costUsd": 0.008027,
      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended here. A used motorbike is bought with a twenty thousand dollar loan, at seven point two per cent a year, compounded monthly, repaid at four hundred dollars a month. A quick guess is twenty thousand divided by four hundred, which is fifty repayments. But the first month's interest is a hundred and twenty dollars, so only two hundred and eighty dollars of that repayment pays off the bike. Is it fifty repayments, about sixty, or more than seventy? Make a guess. Here's the race. Without interest, the loan would be gone at fifty. With interest, it takes sixty."
    },
