      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 106,
      "outputTokens": 829,
      "costUsd": 0.007514,
      "pronunciationText": "So how do we find that exactly? Start with what repaid means. After the last repayment, the balance is zero. And we already have a formula for the balance after n repayments. A sub n equals P times one plus r to the n, minus M times one plus r to the n, minus one, all over r. Here P is twenty thousand, r is zero point zero zero six, and M is four hundred. So we set A sub n equal to zero, and this time the unknown is n."
    },
