      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 150,
      "outputTokens": 1016,
      "costUsd": 0.009219,
      "pronunciationText": "Multiply both sides by r, and the first month's interest, one hundred and twenty dollars, appears. Gather the powers, and you get two hundred and eighty times one point zero zero six to the n equals four hundred. So one point zero zero six to the n is ten sevenths. Take logs of both sides, and n comes down from the power. n is log of ten sevenths over log one point zero zero six, about fifty-nine point six two. This only works because four hundred is more than the interest. If it only matched the interest, we'd divide by zero, and the balance would never change. If it were less, the right side would be negative, and no power could equal it."
