      "outputTokens": 959,
      "costUsd": 0.0087035,
      "pronunciationText": "Fifty-nine point six two repayments isn't possible, so which whole number? After fifty-nine repayments, there's still two hundred and forty-eight dollars thirty-eight owing. So the loan needs sixty repayments, and the last one is smaller, just two hundred and forty-nine dollars eighty-seven, once a month's interest is added. Always round the term up. The total actually paid is fifty-nine lots of four hundred, plus that last repayment, which is twenty-three thousand, eight hundred and forty-nine dollars eighty-seven cents. Take away the twenty thousand borrowed, and the bike cost three thousand, eight hundred and forty-nine dollars eighty-seven in interest."
