      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 106,
      "outputTokens": 826,
      "costUsd": 0.007487,
      "pronunciationText": "Now turn it around. Say you want the bike paid off in exactly four years, which is forty-eight repayments. What should each repayment be? Set A forty-eight equal to zero, and now M is the unknown. Add the repayment term to both sides, so the loan's growth equals the repayments' growth. Then multiply both sides by r, and divide by the bracket. That gives M equals P r times one plus r to the n, all over one plus r to the n, minus one."
    },
