      "costUsd": 0.007775000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "One more question. At four hundred dollars a month, how much is still owed on the bike after two years? That's after twenty-four repayments, so use the same formula with n equal to twenty-four. Twenty thousand times one point zero zero six to the twenty-four, minus four hundred times the bracket, over zero point zero zero six, gives twelve thousand, seven hundred and ninety-five dollars twenty-six cents. That's forty per cent of the time, but only about thirty-six per cent of the loan is paid off, because the early repayments carried the most interest."
